From: Franco Venturi <fventuri@comcast.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: macb: fcfb zero-copy UDP TX (in-kernel, "zcudp")

Add an in-kernel zero-copy UDP TX path to the Zynq-7000 GEM (macb) to break the
~28-31k pps ceiling of userspace sendmmsg(MSG_ZEROCOPY), whose per-datagram
get_user_pages cost caps fcfb's 40k rec/s stream and drops ~25-30% of blocks at
high W.  The vendor stack proves the same GEM sustains 40k+ pps at zero overflow
by building frames in-kernel; this is fcfb's adaptation.

This is NOT a new driver: the new file macb_zcudp.c compiles into macb.o and
runs as part of macb.  zcudp_probe() is called from macb_probe(); the ioctls
arrive through macb's new .ndo_siocdevprivate; and the transmit descriptors it
builds share queue[0]'s HW ring with normal macb traffic (SSH + TCP control).
It lives in its own file only to keep the TX engine out of the 6200-line
macb_main.c.  ("zcudp" = zero-copy UDP.)

zcudp is a generic raw datagram-batch transmitter driven by SIOCDEVPRIVATE
ioctls 0x89f1..0x89f7.  The userspace fcfb_server keeps all framing/packing and
the frontier chase; per datagram it hands the kernel the inline fcfb header
bytes plus 1-2 payload fragments as {ring phys, len} into the u-dma-buf PL ring.
The kernel prepends a templated Eth/IPv4/UDP header (IP length + checksum
patched per datagram; UDP checksum 0, legal for IPv4) and DMAs each frame out
GEM queue[0] as a header BD (coherent buffer) + payload BD(s) pointing straight
at ring phys - no copy, no get_user_pages, no socket path.

Unlike the vendor engine it has no block-fragmentation, no app header, and no
in-kernel resend ring (fcfb's frontier chase + client seq gate handle loss),
and it drains SYNCHRONOUSLY with window flow-control on the caller's thread
(no kthread) because the fcfb ring is ephemeral - the PL overwrites it
continuously, so a decoupled queue could ship already-clobbered records.

zcudp BDs carry no skb and are not dma_map'd, so macb_tx_complete recycles them
via the zcudp_flag tag instead of dev_kfree_skb/dma_unmap, and zcudp_tx_inflight
tracks shared-ring occupancy across both producers.

Signed-off-by: Franco Venturi <fventuri@comcast.net>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb.h
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb.h	2026-09-27 13:49:45.849464059 -0400
